WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.247 --> 00:00:01.929
- Just takin' a little selfie.

00:00:01.929 --> 00:00:04.012
(laughs)

00:00:05.293 --> 00:00:08.210
(funky horn music)

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.668
- I am recreating Michael
Jackson's Thriller.

00:00:12.668 --> 00:00:15.720
- I will be recreating Missy
Elliott's Under Construction.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.694
- The Score by the Fugees.

00:00:18.694 --> 00:00:21.781
- Diana Ross's debut solo album.

00:00:21.781 --> 00:00:22.975
- Dirty Mind by Prince.

00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:24.135
- The album cover I'm recreating

00:00:24.135 --> 00:00:27.565
is the Janet Jackson self entitled album.

00:00:27.565 --> 00:00:29.972
- Solange Knowles, A Seat at the Table.

00:00:29.972 --> 00:00:32.668
- We got Outkast, the album is Stankonia.

00:00:32.668 --> 00:00:34.614
- Mike is going to be Big Boi.

00:00:34.614 --> 00:00:35.548
- Yep.

00:00:35.548 --> 00:00:37.726
And Richard's gonna be Andre 3000.

00:00:37.726 --> 00:00:39.068
- My hair's a little short right now,

00:00:39.068 --> 00:00:41.735
so am I gonna get to wear a wig?

00:00:43.122 --> 00:00:43.955
Alright.

00:00:49.814 --> 00:00:52.731
(rhythm and blues)

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.129
- On the album cover you see the boom box,

00:00:58.129 --> 00:01:00.526
you see the graffiti, the
wall in the background,

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.322
her on the trash can, her kecks,

00:01:02.322 --> 00:01:04.218
like she's giving you that old school

00:01:04.218 --> 00:01:06.288
gritty hip hop feel, and letting you know.

00:01:06.288 --> 00:01:08.578
This is an album that I'm paying homage

00:01:08.578 --> 00:01:11.439
to the greats, paying
homage to the hip hop roots.

00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:14.412
- The Score was actually the
first album I ever bought.

00:01:14.412 --> 00:01:15.564
I was six!

00:01:15.564 --> 00:01:17.488
I used my little chore
money, I'll never forget,

00:01:17.488 --> 00:01:19.427
I asked my cousin, cos
she had the cassette

00:01:19.427 --> 00:01:20.943
and she wouldn't let me borrow it.

00:01:20.943 --> 00:01:22.006
- When I look at the album cover

00:01:22.006 --> 00:01:25.467
it's just like a celebration of blackness.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:26.649
- I think it's really powerful

00:01:26.649 --> 00:01:28.859
because it's like this black woman,

00:01:28.859 --> 00:01:30.257
she has the clips in her hair

00:01:30.257 --> 00:01:32.056
and her hair isn't pressed or anything,

00:01:32.056 --> 00:01:34.127
it's natural, and she's just like,

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:37.550
"I don't care how I'm
supposed to be lookin',

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.978
"This is how I'm doing it."

00:01:38.978 --> 00:01:39.939
- This album cover is everything,

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:42.395
those pictures are everything
and they're so powerful.

00:01:42.395 --> 00:01:45.154
It created a whole new world, kind of,

00:01:45.154 --> 00:01:46.809
for a lot of female artists.

00:01:46.809 --> 00:01:48.753
- When I first saw it, I just remember

00:01:48.753 --> 00:01:50.765
just like being so drawn to it,

00:01:50.765 --> 00:01:52.560
because there's just
something very alluring

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.701
about Diana Ross in general, but like

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.732
especially on this cover
because there's like

00:01:56.732 --> 00:01:59.736
this subtle confidence
that draws me to her.

00:01:59.736 --> 00:02:02.151
- We used to go to the
record store in my home town,

00:02:02.151 --> 00:02:04.542
and I remember they had it like blown up,

00:02:04.542 --> 00:02:06.840
like a big, like a big poster,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.470
but I just remember thinkin' like,

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.411
this dude is cool as hell.

00:02:10.411 --> 00:02:12.346
He is lookin' at me and sayin',

00:02:12.346 --> 00:02:15.539
do not try me, do not fuck with me,

00:02:15.539 --> 00:02:18.544
because I will take your girl.

00:02:18.544 --> 00:02:20.017
- I remember when I first saw it,

00:02:20.017 --> 00:02:21.598
I really didn't think anything of it,

00:02:21.598 --> 00:02:23.689
but later in life, as I got older,

00:02:23.689 --> 00:02:25.076
I looked at it and I was just like,

00:02:25.076 --> 00:02:26.472
oh crap, it's an American flag

00:02:26.472 --> 00:02:28.735
but you have the black background

00:02:28.735 --> 00:02:30.974
and then the white stars on top of it,

00:02:30.974 --> 00:02:32.799
which for me means like,

00:02:32.799 --> 00:02:35.702
America was kind of built on
the backs of black people.

00:02:35.702 --> 00:02:37.583
- Yeah, that's my favorite
part of the cover,

00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:39.127
because I feel like the cover itself

00:02:39.127 --> 00:02:42.209
is just like them being
like, this is our America.

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:44.185
- The first time I saw this album cover

00:02:44.185 --> 00:02:48.428
I thought that he is hung over,
or waking up from a party,

00:02:48.428 --> 00:02:52.470
and he's simultaneously hot
and cold at the same time.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:55.233
If I saw somebody wearing
a biker jacket and a Speedo

00:02:55.233 --> 00:02:57.707
I'd be like, what's going
on in this guy's mind,

00:02:57.707 --> 00:03:00.213
he seems a little confused, but confident,

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.843
looking right at the camera.

00:03:01.843 --> 00:03:03.926
(laughs)

00:03:06.521 --> 00:03:08.547
- I'm really excited to recreate the look

00:03:08.547 --> 00:03:10.380
with the natural hair.

00:03:11.597 --> 00:03:13.595
- I'm hyped, I'm not nervous at all.

00:03:13.595 --> 00:03:14.879
- We cutes, though.

00:03:14.879 --> 00:03:16.379
- Too cute, honey.

00:03:17.306 --> 00:03:18.398
- Let's get weird, guys.

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:19.231
- Alright!

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:20.064
(laughs)

00:03:20.064 --> 00:03:21.574
- There's always been
in the back of my mind

00:03:21.574 --> 00:03:22.996
all these insecurities, so I don't know

00:03:22.996 --> 00:03:24.313
if this might be a way

00:03:24.313 --> 00:03:26.755
of sort of letting those insecurities go,

00:03:26.755 --> 00:03:28.556
or if it might help me.

00:03:28.556 --> 00:03:30.163
(laughs)

00:03:30.163 --> 00:03:31.844
This is my Janet boobs.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.052
- I am excited to dress up

00:03:33.052 --> 00:03:36.157
in a Speedo and a biker jacket at work.

00:03:36.157 --> 00:03:39.179
- I want everybody to
keep movin' for this one.

00:03:39.179 --> 00:03:41.946
I am excited to recreate
this because she is one

00:03:41.946 --> 00:03:45.144
of the most iconic artists
in American history,

00:03:45.144 --> 00:03:47.382
and she is a black woman as well,

00:03:47.382 --> 00:03:51.454
and she's like one of the
first huge black divas

00:03:51.454 --> 00:03:54.367
and I feel like she basically
created the template

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:58.001
that all of these other
pop stars basically go by.

00:03:58.001 --> 00:03:59.398
- I'm fuckin' excited, oh I cursed!

00:03:59.398 --> 00:04:00.745
- Yeah, I am too.

00:04:00.745 --> 00:04:03.982
I'm excited and nervous
about wearing leather pants.

00:04:03.982 --> 00:04:05.105
(laughs)

00:04:05.105 --> 00:04:06.901
- I'm assuming I'm gonna
have to like wear a wig.

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:09.318
He's got like the permed out.

00:04:11.005 --> 00:04:13.321
- See, you can wear a wig, but I can't.

00:04:13.321 --> 00:04:14.571
There's no way.

00:04:15.637 --> 00:04:19.224
- I'm definitely excited to
kinda step back into this moment

00:04:19.224 --> 00:04:21.856
that Michael did, I guess
he was like 24 or 25,

00:04:21.856 --> 00:04:24.679
he defined the industry,
like let's be real.

00:04:24.679 --> 00:04:27.200
- Oh my God, you basically
killin' that shit!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.955
- You know I never thought
this day would come,

00:04:28.955 --> 00:04:30.312
but now that it's here I feel

00:04:30.312 --> 00:04:32.475
that Missy and I will
finally be the best friends

00:04:32.475 --> 00:04:34.100
that we've been destined to be.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.229
So Melissa, when this comes
out, when this is ready,

00:04:37.229 --> 00:04:39.878
you know, let's get
lunch, let's get drinks.

00:04:39.878 --> 00:04:40.969
Love you.

00:04:40.969 --> 00:04:42.052
- Wooo hoooo!

00:04:43.496 --> 00:04:45.641
Solange, what were you thinkin'?

00:04:45.641 --> 00:04:47.940
I think that it was very
specific to women of color,

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.277
and women of color who
get their hair done.

00:04:50.277 --> 00:04:51.990
We all know where to buy those clips,

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.940
and we all know where our
hairdresser keeps those clips.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.839
Just like seeing that, there is already

00:04:56.839 --> 00:05:00.589
an instant connection
with me and my friends.

00:05:01.428 --> 00:05:03.783
My parents are gonna love this.

00:05:03.783 --> 00:05:06.639
- Yeah, her brows up with the rest.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.281
- They're totally just
surrounded by shadows,

00:05:09.281 --> 00:05:13.448
I think that speaks a lot
to the black experience.

00:05:15.703 --> 00:05:17.477
But they're shining beyond the shadows,

00:05:17.477 --> 00:05:18.933
they're shining through
it and you see them.

00:05:18.933 --> 00:05:20.169
- Ooooh, controversy.

00:05:20.169 --> 00:05:22.340
- You see all the things that
our people are surrounded by.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.173
- Yeah.

00:05:26.873 --> 00:05:28.314
- If this album cover could talk,

00:05:28.314 --> 00:05:29.625
it would just be like,

00:05:29.625 --> 00:05:31.720
"Fuck you, this is who I am

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.231
"and this is what I came to do."

00:05:33.231 --> 00:05:34.750
- Black is beautiful, I know that

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.692
and I will stand by it every day.

00:05:36.692 --> 00:05:39.813
But to have an artist on
such a large platform as his,

00:05:39.813 --> 00:05:42.444
and to be able to use his platform

00:05:42.444 --> 00:05:43.958
to make a statement like that,

00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:48.125
that goes leaps and bounds,
and that says so much.

00:05:52.281 --> 00:05:54.668
The bob, and the attitude,
and the confidence,

00:05:54.668 --> 00:05:56.439
I think we should all have that every day,

00:05:56.439 --> 00:05:59.415
cos as Michael shows you,
it can take you places.

00:05:59.415 --> 00:06:02.050
- Sorry Diana, can you
move back a little, okay?

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:04.717
- I just love inspiring figures.

00:06:05.982 --> 00:06:09.372
She is definitely like a huge one,

00:06:09.372 --> 00:06:13.552
in not only music history
but also black history.

00:06:13.552 --> 00:06:15.052
- Okay, unhand me!

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:18.273
(laughs)

00:06:18.273 --> 00:06:19.409
I don't know you!

00:06:19.409 --> 00:06:21.319
If the album could talk,

00:06:21.319 --> 00:06:24.676
I'd probably think that it would just say,

00:06:24.676 --> 00:06:26.650
I am a woman, this is me,

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:29.733
and I am fierce, powerful and strong.

00:06:31.059 --> 00:06:32.636
- Haven't worn a Speedo in a while.

00:06:32.636 --> 00:06:33.636
Ever, maybe.

00:06:35.315 --> 00:06:36.365
What is feminine, right?

00:06:36.365 --> 00:06:37.968
And I think that it's kind of funny,

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:40.491
because now in 2017 it's like gender

00:06:40.491 --> 00:06:42.810
is such like an old concept,

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.417
and so I think that kind
of blurring those lines

00:06:45.417 --> 00:06:48.250
is a little bit ahead of his time.

00:06:49.479 --> 00:06:52.062
(funky guitar)

00:06:53.865 --> 00:06:56.818
I can but I don't want to.

00:06:56.818 --> 00:06:59.424
- You should definitely go
back to your desk like that.

00:06:59.424 --> 00:07:02.056
- She laid the foundation
for me as a black girl

00:07:02.056 --> 00:07:03.806
to hold my head high.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:12.063
To be confident with whatever I wear,

00:07:12.063 --> 00:07:16.687
whatever I look like,
and how I present myself.

00:07:16.687 --> 00:07:19.270
(funky guitar)

